 dict(id='sanxie',category='investment',type=['笔试案例 · 杠杆收购','Written-test case · Leveraged buyout'],year='2026',name=['三协电机：回报背后的条件','Sanxie Motor: Conditions behind the returns'],sub=['LBO 模型、投资备忘录与动态情景分析','LBO model, investment memorandum and dynamic scenarios'],desc=['28.63% 的模型 IRR，依赖经营修复与追加资本。把回报拆解成可验证的假设。','A modeled 28.63% IRR depends on operating recovery and follow-on equity. Translating returns into testable assumptions.'],cover='lbo',tags=['28.63% modeled IRR','3.40× MOIC','10-page memo'],files=[('阅读投资备忘录','Read the investment memo','sanxie-memo.pdf'),('下载 Excel 模型','Download Excel model','sanxie-model.xlsx')],sections=[
 ('案例交易与回报','Case transaction and returns','案例假设以每股 13 元收购三协电机，完全稀释股数 103.33 百万股，股权购买价 1343.29 百万元，初始发起人股本 886.90 百万元，收购债务 413.00 百万元。进出场 EV/EBITDA 均为 14.91 倍。模型 IRR 为 28.63%，MOIC 为 3.40 倍。','The case assumes a RMB 13 per-share offer, 103.33 million fully diluted shares, RMB 1,343.29 million equity purchase price, RMB 886.90 million initial sponsor equity and RMB 413.00 million acquisition debt. Entry and exit EV/EBITDA are both 14.91×. Modeled IRR is 28.63% and MOIC is 3.40×.'),
 ('经营质量与产业位置','Operating quality and industry position','分析 3D 打印、光伏跟踪、工业自动化、纺织、安防和机器人需求；将设备需求、单机电机价值量、供应份额与 ASP 联系起来，考察客户议价、原料价格、产品内毛利变化和应收质量。','Analyzes 3D printing, solar tracking, industrial automation, textile, surveillance and robotics demand. Links equipment demand, motor content, sourcing share and ASP, and examines OEM bargaining power, materials, within-product margins and receivable quality.'),
 ('现金流与追加资本','Cash flow and follow-on equity','前三年需追加发起人股本 102.56 百万元，分别为 61.18、37.46 和 3.92 百万元。模型连接经营预测、债务摊还、最低现金、现金清扫、股本追加和退出价值；按完整股东现金流计算 IRR。','The first three years require RMB 102.56 million of follow-on equity: 61.18, 37.46 and 3.92 million. The model links operating forecasts, amortization, minimum cash, cash sweeps, equity calls and exit value, calculating IRR from full sponsor cash flows.'),
 ('投资判断与敏感性','Investment view and sensitivities','备忘录建议进入针对性尽调，在有约束力报价前验证融资与经营恢复。检验退出 EBITDA、毛利率、退出倍数、收入增速、进入溢价、资本开支及营运资金。EBITDA 增长占正向价值创造的 92.3%。数值为案例条件性测算，非实际投资业绩。','The memorandum recommends focused diligence, verifying financing and operating recovery before a binding offer. Sensitivities cover exit EBITDA, gross margin, exit multiple, revenue growth, entry premium, capex and working capital. EBITDA growth contributes 92.3% of positive value creation. These are conditional case outputs, not realized performance.')]),
